  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="114a-7ed5-4631-41fa" name="Late Medieval Burgundy (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>LATE MEDIEVAL BURGUNDY &amp; BURGUNDIAN ORDONNANCE 1453-1477 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.60-61). Special Formations: Ordonnance Longbowmen may be in a Combined Formation with Ordonnance Pikemen. Mounted Coustilliers may be in the rear ranks of a Combined Formation with Mounted Knights/Ordonnance Gendarmes or Mounted Feudal Knights. Household Foot, Dismounted Knights/Ordonnance Gendarmes, Dismounted Feudal Knights, or Dismounted Coustilliers may be in Mixed Order with Archers/Ordonnance Longbowmen, Crossbowmen, or Handgunners. One unit of Archers/Ordonnance Longbowmen or Handgunners may be skirmishers for every 1,000 army points. Wars of the Roses English allies documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Late Medieval Burgundy &amp; Burgundian Ordonnance]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-75%, Infantry 25-75%. Artillery: one gun per 500 army points, bought from the Infantry allocation. Allies: 0-25% may be Wars of the Roses English (documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
